# snapshot-evidence-cell's starts of core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh (BL-879 grammar). Every other drive is in
# process: run.sh asks vab_main through vab_ip. One cli cell per distinct CLI outcome (exit 0, exit 1), each started as
# FXCELL=<id> bash in vab_eqv() and compared byte for byte with the in-process call on the same input.
cli core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh cli-vab-pass
cli core/scripts/validate-artifact-budget.sh cli-vab-refuse
# The gate-log fallback of vab_main starts its sibling classifier, which starts sprint-status.sh; run.sh tags each call that takes the fallback with its own ordinal (FXCELL=e2e-scope-chain-<n>), one start per cell.
e2e core/scripts/check-owed-derivations.sh e2e-scope-chain-1 why=the validator's gate-log fallback starts the scope classifier as a program (bash "$gl_tool" --scope-batch) from inside an in-process vab_main, a call that is no start, so no nested row covers it, and no shim can answer it because inproc_run strips every function the subject did not define
